MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE...1008 MB...29.77 INCHES
 
 
WATCHES AND WARNINGS
--------------------
There are no coastal watches or warnings in effect.
 
Interests in the Hawaiian Islands should monitor the progress of
Fausto.
 
 
DISCUSSION AND OUTLOOK
----------------------
At 1100 PM HST (0900 UTC), the center of Tropical Depression Fausto 
was located near latitude 23.3 North, longitude 154.5 West. The 
depression is moving toward the west-northwest near 12 mph (19 km/h) 
and this motion is expected to continue for the next couple of days. 
On the forecast track, Fausto will pass north of the Hawaiian 
Islands through late Wednesday.
 
Maximum sustained winds have decreased to near 35 mph (55 km/h) with 
higher gusts. Additional weakening is likely, and Fausto is expected 
to become a post-tropical remnant low on Wednesday.
 
The estimated minimum central pressure is 1008 mb (29.77 inches).
 
 
HAZARDS AFFECTING LAND
----------------------
Key messages for Fausto can be found in the Tropical Cyclone
Discussion under AWIPS header HFOTCDCP1 and WMO header WTPA41 PHFO.
 
SURF: Surf generated by Fausto is building westward across the
Hawaiian Islands along exposed east-facing shores and will
remain dangerous on Wednesday as Fausto passes north of the
islands.  Large surf and strong currents will lead to dangerous
conditions along exposed shores.  Please consult products from your
local weather office.
 
 
